WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.820
From dragon flame foreshadowing to easter
eggs revealing how fan favourite fairies Tecna

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.990
and Flora will appear, Fate: The Winx Saga
has a stack of secrets hidden in every episode.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:14.960
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm uncovering all the magical details you

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.610
might have missed in the first season of Netflix's
live-action adaptation of Winx Club,

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:24.520
including the secret twist that Ms Dowling's
fate in the finale may not be what it seems.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.350
We will of course be talking spoilers, so
take care.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:32.289
Although the new series initially downplays
fans' expectations of getting to see the Winx

00:00:32.289 --> 00:00:33.300
with fairy wings..

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.680
"Just kinda bummed I didn't see a single pair
of wings."

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.120
"Well, we had wings in the past.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.910
As we've evolved, transformation magic has
been lost."

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:44.000
..the red butterfly on the lamp that Bloom
brings with her to Alfea is a clever bit of

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.570
foreshadowing to her big transformation in
the finale when she sprouts wings as she unleashes

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.200
the power of the dragon flame inside her.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.790
And that scene pays homage to elements of
Bloom's original Winx Club transformation,

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.040
albeit with some notable differences.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.220
The fire that licks around her as she goes
full fairy is similar to the animation, although

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.899
in Winx Club the fire wrapping around Bloom
is accompanied by a costume change.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:10.890
If you're disappointed by the Netflix show's
lack of costume change, remember that Bloom

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:15.390
has only just discovered the Dragon Flame,
and as her powers grow in the future, her

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.499
transformations may well become bigger and
better.

00:01:17.499 --> 00:01:21.670
And hopefully, the other Winx Suite members
will also get wings too like in the animated

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:22.670
show.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.749
By the way, in the original Winx Club, the
Dragon Flame also gave Bloom healing abilities,

00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:31.290
including the time she was able to save Sky
after a fatal attack;

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.779
and it appears that in Fate, Bloom has also
acquired a similar ability when she heals

00:01:35.779 --> 00:01:39.350
a cut on Sky's face just by touching it.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:43.509
Another big moment from the final episode
comes when Rosalind abruptly kills Farah with

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:45.189
her magic by snapping her neck.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:49.739
This was an unexpected and shocking moment,
but also a somewhat underwhelming way for

00:01:49.739 --> 00:01:52.919
a powerful fairy like Ms Dowling to exit the
show.

00:01:52.919 --> 00:01:57.159
If you're a Farah fan though, you can take
solace in the subtle hint you might have missed

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:01.450
in the scene that suggests the former headmistress
may still be alive.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:05.959
Notice how Farah's eyes light up just before
Rosalind attacks her, suggesting she may be

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:10.810
drawing on her own magic to protect herself
against a likely attack from her nemesis.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:15.260
Farah's dead body may simply be an illusion
she's cast to fool Rosalind, like many of

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.459
the other illusions we've seen fairies cast
in the show.

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:22.709
And if you're at all sceptical, then just
remember that Sky's father Andreas was brought

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:27.329
back from the dead despite the seemingly lethal
blow that Silva landed on him.

00:02:27.329 --> 00:02:31.580
And let's not forget that handy healing power
that Bloom has either.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:37.379
The casting of Terra and Musa has been problematic
given how it erased both Latin and Asian representation

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:42.170
in the new series, making this show's main
cast less diverse than the original noughties

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.170
animation.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.049
There is, however, a tease to a potential
resolution for fans disappointed at the lack

00:02:47.049 --> 00:02:51.430
of Flora in the series when Terra reveals
some more details about her family to Musa.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.250
"I've got this cousin called Flora, and my
mum's called Rose."

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.659
The Flora namedrop hopefully means that the
OG Winx Club nature fairy who was modelled

00:02:58.659 --> 00:03:02.760
on Jennifer Lopez will be introduced in a
future season.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.620
Another missing founding fairy from the animated
series is Tecna, the fairy of technology.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.129
However, there's a clue in the first season
that might have revealed her or somebody closely

00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.270
related to her.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:17.840
In the third episode, when Bloom is studying
some of the Alfea yearbooks, the camera deliberately

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.900
goes in close on one of the pages, lingering
on it for several seconds.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.330
Interestingly, one of the names on the page,
"Devon Walker", is described as a Science

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.330
Fair winner.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:32.280
It looks like this description refers to this
former alumna of Alfea here, who also appears

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:37.260
in the centre of this group photo, and who
Bloom commented was a "Farah Fawcett" lookalike

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.030
when she saw her in a school photo on one
of the walls.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.590
The show seems to be calling attention to
this character, and the fact that she was

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:48.290
particularly skilled at science could imply
that this is Tecna, or if not Tecna herself,

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.239
then someone related to her, for example,
her mother.

00:03:51.239 --> 00:03:54.530
Of course, it's possible that this is just
a tease to a brand new original character

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:59.620
that will be introduced later on, but either
way it seems likely she will have some significance

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.400
to a future storyline.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.659
Also mentioned on the page is somebody called
"Sparta West 'Red'" and if you've any theories

00:04:05.659 --> 00:04:08.840
about Tecna or either of these two characters,
comment below!

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.680
When Bloom meets Rosalind for the first time,
the show seems to imply that the voices Bloom

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.870
has been hearing calling to her have been
Rosalind's all along.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.530
[whispering] Hello, Bloom.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:22.490
However, if you go back and listen to the
ghostly voices that Bloom originally heard

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.630
calling to her, they sound quite different
to Rosalind's voice.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:31.050
[whispering voices] Bloom, Bloom..

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:35.449
These may actually be a hint and a tease to
Daphne who was a type of spirit guardian and

00:04:35.449 --> 00:04:37.900
sister to Bloom in Winx Club.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.060
Similar to the mysterious voice calling to
Bloom in the new show, Daphne's ghost also

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.910
called to Bloom in Winx Club to come and find
her.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.490
"I'm all around you Bloom.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.550
I'm within you Bloom.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.850
I'll show you."

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:53.850
"Woh!

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:54.850
Daphne!"

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.500
Daphne was also once a guardian of the Dragon
Flame and so if she appears in the show, she'll

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.920
likely have a part to play in helping Bloom
learn about that power.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:07.770
Alfea's resident bad girl Beatrix may be an
air fairy, however, her name is a reference

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:11.289
to the villainous Trix sisters from Winx Club,
who were witches.

00:05:11.289 --> 00:05:16.790
Beatrix also says that she's from Aster Dell,
which was apparently a village of Blood Witches,

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:20.780
suggesting it's possible that Beatrix will
actually turn out to be a witch in the show,

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.410
rather than a fairy.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:27.990
And although Beatrix appears to combine various
attributes of the three OG Trix, Icy, Darcy

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:32.540
and Stormy, it wouldn't surprise me if she
discovers she has a couple of villainous sisters

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.289
or relations in a future season.

00:05:35.289 --> 00:05:39.560
And if you were ever in any doubt that bad
boy Riven would end up joining Beatrix on

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.289
the Dark Side, the infamous book on his desk
is a dead giveaway.

00:05:43.289 --> 00:05:47.870
The overall theme of "The Prince" by Machiavelli,
that it's justifiable to act in an immoral

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:52.070
way in order to achieve political goals,
also points to some of the themes in the first

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:57.070
season such as Rosalind lying about evacuating
Aster Dell so she could destroy the Blood

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.069
Witches living there as well as the Burned
Ones.

00:06:00.069 --> 00:06:03.729
Another little detail about Riven you might
have missed comes in the final episode when

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.830
he meets Rosalind for the first time.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:10.770
Notice how both his and Dale's eyes light
up as she enters the room, which could suggest

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:15.100
that they have some latent magical abilities,
or the way that Rosalind's eyes glowed at

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:19.900
the same time could imply that she's cast
a spell on them to pull them over to her side

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.009
as she takes control over the school.

00:06:22.009 --> 00:06:26.280
There's a hint that we could see some of the
more interesting powers Aisha had in the animated

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.400
series in Fate.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.590
For clues, let's take a look at the scene
where Farah is explaining to Aisha about her

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:32.850
water-based powers.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:35.490
"A mass of water, is persistent and reliable.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.090
A drop of water..
is unpredictable.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.090
Vague.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.090
Amorphous.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.090
Can you isolate it?

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:44.190
Can you maintain that which fights form?"

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:48.551
Farah's description of water as "amorphous"
could be a reference to "Morphix", the name

00:06:48.551 --> 00:06:53.159
of Aisha's power source in Winx Club and a
magical, malleable substance which the fairy

00:06:53.159 --> 00:06:56.580
can create by rearranging water molecules.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.199
"Morphix Cloud!"

00:06:59.199 --> 00:07:02.900
I'm not sure whether the Fate showrunners
will go there, but there were some really

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:08.520
cool things like Aisha's Morphix Surfboard
that could be awesome to see in live action.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.439
"Morphix Surfboard!"

00:07:10.439 --> 00:07:14.789
By the way, there's also a hint in Fate that
Aisha might be a princess like she is in Winx

00:07:14.789 --> 00:07:19.020
Club when Stella tells Bloom to ask Aisha
about what it means to lose a Crown Jewel.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:20.919
"That might not mean much to a First Worlder.

00:07:20.919 --> 00:07:23.699
Feel free to ask your suite-mate how big of
a screw-up that is."

00:07:23.699 --> 00:07:26.129
"Almost as big as giving it to her in the
first place."

00:07:26.129 --> 00:07:30.389
Another change from Winx Club is Musa being
a mind fairy rather than a fairy of music.

00:07:30.389 --> 00:07:34.199
There are, however, a few references in the
new series to her musical background in the

00:07:34.199 --> 00:07:37.539
animation, from the DJ poster on the wall
by her bed,

00:07:37.539 --> 00:07:41.380
to how she listens to music on her headphones
whenever she wants to drown out reading other

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:45.340
people's emotions, to the fact that she tells
Riven she was once a dancer.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.629
"I wouldn't expect a mind fairy to have such
good moves."

00:07:47.629 --> 00:07:49.439
"I used to be a dancer."

00:07:49.439 --> 00:07:54.100
Fashion was a huge part of Winx Club and fans
of that aspect of the OG show will likely

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.690
be disappointed with the costuming on Fate.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:08:01.009
There is perhaps a small nod to Winx Club
fashion though when Bloom is surprised at

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:03.320
how often Stella changes her clothes each
day.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:05.090
"So, a casual thing you're changing for?"

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.000
"People have seen me in this outfit already.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.890
They'll expect something different.

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.410
People expect you to wear multiple outfits
a day?"

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:15.009
And there's another neat little homage to
the OG series when Bloom reveals that she

00:08:15.009 --> 00:08:21.150
was born in 2004, a reference to how Winx
Club first premiered on Italian TV in that

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:22.150
year.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:25.680
And in case you didn't know, Abigail Cowen
who plays Bloom also starred in Netflix's

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.870
Chilling Adventures of Sabrina as one of the
three Weird Sisters,

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:32.599
and if you're fan of that show, check out
my video with all the best easter eggs and

00:08:32.599 --> 00:08:35.150
things you missed in the final season of Sabrina.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:38.190
Tap here to watch that or follow the link
in the video description.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:43.270
So what did you think of Fate: The Winx Saga,
and how it changed from the animated series?

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.200
And do you have any theories on what you'd
like to see in Season 2?

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.450
Leave all your thoughts and comments down
below.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:51.950
And if you enjoyed this, then a thumbs-up
is hugely appreciated!

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:56.590
Tap left for my next Netflix video including
a full breakdown of the Sabrina series finale

00:08:56.590 --> 00:09:00.500
and a potential Part 5, or tap right for something
else you're sure to like.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.610
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.900
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

